WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:06.420
Last July I was in Rome.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:11.540
I walked from my hotel
to the Trevi Fountain

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:16.260
on the cobbled streets
lined with beautiful cafes,

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:19.780
bustling with residents and travelers,

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:23.140
drinking their espressos
and cheering and greeting each other.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:29.340
Small souvenir shops selling
beautiful replicas of the Colosseum,

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:32.420
the Sistine Chapel ceiling paintings.

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:33.700
What an atmosphere.

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:37.300
I soaked it all in,

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:39.500
reached the Trevi Fountain,

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:43.460
grabbed my favorite pistachio gelato

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:46.060
and looked at the marvelous views.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:48.660
A perfect Roman holiday.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:52.380
Suddenly my alarm rang

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:54.420
and I woke up from my dream.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:57.740
I was in Rome.

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:01.580
I did walk from my hotel
to the Trevi Fountain.

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:04.700
But I felt rushed.

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:09.140
The cafes were crowded.

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:12.020
People had to even queue outside.

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:16.020
The shopkeepers had no time
to entertain visitors.

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:19.340
I reached the Trevi Fountain

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:23.380
and forgot [to] grab
my favorite pistachio gelato

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:25.260
or find a bench to sit.

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:28.260
I couldn't get to the steps.

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:32.860
Thousands and thousands
of people all around.

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:35.300
Have you felt the same way?

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:39.420
When you reach your dream destination,

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:42.500
you feel as if it has been overrun.

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:45.860
You feel as if it has become
a selfie queue.

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:48.020
I had the same feeling.

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:49.900
And this is not an isolated incident.

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:54.500
I had the same exact experience in Tokyo

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:57.620
when I went there
during the cherry blossom season.

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:03.180
Tourists crowd every park in the city

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:05.060
to get a glimpse of the famous sakura.

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:11.940
I asked a resident: “How does [you] feel
seeing so many tourists all around?”

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:17.260
He told me that he doesn't bring
his family anymore

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:18.940
for a picnic under the sakura.

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:22.300
That response broke my heart.

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:27.780
We are loving our favorite
destinations to death.

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:30.660
We are overrunning them.

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:34.740
And residents are pushing back

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:36.860
because it's impacting their livability.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:41.220
Their cost of living is increasing,
congestion on the road,

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:44.420
rental prices, food prices.

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:45.940
They are pushing back.

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:48.820
And they're pushing back
like in Barcelona,

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:51.260
with the graffiti
asking tourists to go home.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:55.420
In Barcelona, in Italy, in Portugal,

00:02:56.740 --> 00:02:58.660
residents are pushing back.

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:02.100
I have been researching
the travel industry

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:03.700
for [the] last 20 years

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:08.380
and my two research subjects,
the residents and the travelers,

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:11.180
are on a collision course
like never before.

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:15.060
We have a travel crisis.

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:20.940
The travel industry employs
about 300 million people globally,

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:25.180
and it’s going to be
a $15 trillion industry by 2040.

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:27.740
[It’s] too large, [with] too many

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:30.140
livelihoods at stake for
us to ignore this crisis.

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:33.660
But let me pause and ask you a question.

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:36.660
Why do we travel?

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:38.820
We travel for joy.

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:44.660
Joy by experiencing the diversity
this world has to offer.

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:47.340
Joy by experiencing different lives.

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:49.220
Joy through a shared connection.

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:53.100
My daughter, son and wife are here,

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:57.700
and I want them to experience the same joy
I experienced in my Roman dream.

00:03:57.700 --> 00:04:00.580
I want all of you
to experience the same joy.

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:04.780
We need to bring joy back in travel.

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:08.220
But it's a complex problem.

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:13.180
We have millions of tourists
getting inspired by social media

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:16.900
and planning their travel destinations,
and planning their travel itineraries.

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:20.820
We have the travel industry,
which is looking for short-term profits,

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:24.580
and we have cities who don't know
how to manage the tourist inflow.

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:28.460
There is a path forward, though.

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:33.820
With the use of technology like AI
and simple behavior changes,

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:37.020
we could bring joy back in travel.

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:43.060
Now imagine if we were to make
the entire travel industry's objective,

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:45.900
the airlines, the hotel,
the travel tour operators,

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:51.780
to bring joy to both residents
as well as the travelers.

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:53.900
And they have everything
at their disposal,

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:56.540
from technology to people to skilling.

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:58.660
They will rise to the occasion.

00:04:58.660 --> 00:04:59.980
They will do three things:

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:03.020
one, help manage crowd,

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:05.660
help discover authentic experiences

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:09.100
and help drive a really, really
respectful connection

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:12.380
between the resident and the traveler.

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:13.660
On your last trip,

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:17.540
did you feel rushed?

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:20.140
Did you feel like you were
going through a checklist,

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:22.620
moving from one place to another place?

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:25.620
Did it feel like a chore
or did you feel joy?

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:28.540
We all are super busy

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:32.540
and we all land
to the same destinations

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:34.740
during the same peak season times

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:38.820
without realizing quieter seasons,

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:41.500
quieter times, or hidden paths.

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:43.940
What if technology
could help us figure that out?

00:05:45.140 --> 00:05:48.460
FeelFlorence is an app
by the city of Florence,

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:52.180
which helps do
exactly this for the travelers.

00:05:53.260 --> 00:05:58.060
It uses the data from sensors,
from cameras,

00:05:58.100 --> 00:06:00.900
to understand crowded locations,

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:05.220
and recommends personalized
travel itineraries for tourists.

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:08.740
It sends user alerts
to avoid crowded locations.

00:06:08.740 --> 00:06:10.020
When this happens,

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:13.020
it balances the load,

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:16.340
and it is beneficial
for both the tourists,

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:18.100
as well as the residents.

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:20.580
Cities are going down that path.

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:21.860
Amsterdam.

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:24.740
And even religious cities
like Mecca or Varanasi

00:06:24.740 --> 00:06:28.180
are increasingly using technology
to manage crowd.

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:33.780
What was your last unforgettable trip?

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:39.620
Was it the famous landmark,
[the] Instagrammable picture,

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:41.780
or was it a shared smile with someone?

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:45.300
Or was it a story that somebody told you,

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:46.660
of course, in the backdrop

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:49.700
of beautiful nature
or a beautiful surrounding.

00:06:50.900 --> 00:06:52.820
I asked the same question to my friend.

00:06:54.660 --> 00:06:58.260
She said, "If I ignore
my bachelorette party outside,

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:02.900
my last unforgettable trip was in Vietnam.

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:07.300
A fisherman took me on a boat ride,

00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:10.220
told me stories about Vietnam,

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:13.820
told me stories about the life
he has lived there.

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:15.980
And I cannot forget that."

00:07:16.020 --> 00:07:17.380
What a beautiful connection.

00:07:18.860 --> 00:07:20.140
For me,

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:24.820
it was my experience
in Istanbul, in Turkey,

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:28.060
where a cheerful cafe owner
took interest in me

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:30.980
and told me the history of Turkish tea,

00:07:31.020 --> 00:07:33.180
how to make it and how to drink it.

00:07:33.780 --> 00:07:38.340
Whenever I think about Turkey or Istanbul,
my heart fills with joy.

00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:42.140
This is what we crave.
This is what we seek.

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:46.780
I'm sure some of you
have been stranded at airports

00:07:46.780 --> 00:07:49.140
because of airline disruptions.

00:07:49.180 --> 00:07:50.660
The airline has two options:

00:07:50.660 --> 00:07:54.780
one to check you into [a] hotel
overlooking the terminal,

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:58.060
or maybe organize
a Turkish tea-making workshop.

00:07:58.940 --> 00:08:01.300
Maybe some of us will like it,
and if we like it,

00:08:01.340 --> 00:08:04.020
we will become a loyal customer
of the airline.

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:07.260
Same is the case with hotels.

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:10.460
If hotels can use technology
to give custom concierges,

00:08:11.620 --> 00:08:15.100
which speaks in your language,
curates local suggestions,

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:16.900
helps you discover hidden gems,

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:20.540
and walks along with you,

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:25.380
you will become
a loyal customer of the hotel.

00:08:25.420 --> 00:08:27.780
Imagine the possibilities

00:08:29.660 --> 00:08:34.860
of uncovering authentic experiences
that give us true joy.

00:08:36.380 --> 00:08:38.940
Many residents in the destinations we love

00:08:40.340 --> 00:08:42.540
don’t see the direct benefits
of a traveler.

00:08:44.780 --> 00:08:46.900
They only see the negative side.

00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:50.900
I know we are contributing
to the local economy through our money.

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:53.460
But that may not be enough.

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:59.420
And even if we want to contribute
through our time,

00:08:59.460 --> 00:09:01.020
we don't know how to do it.

00:09:02.420 --> 00:09:05.540
Residents feel like
how I used to feel as a child

00:09:05.580 --> 00:09:08.820
when unexpected guests
arrived in my house,

00:09:08.820 --> 00:09:12.700
especially if they didn't carry
any special gifts for me.

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:14.940
I barely uttered a smile

00:09:14.940 --> 00:09:18.260
and I wished that they [would] leave
as soon as possible.

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:22.060
I'm sure many of you,
if you could find a way

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:24.620
to contribute through your time,
you would.

00:09:25.300 --> 00:09:27.700
Again things are changing on this front.

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:30.380
Golden Volunteer
is an example of a platform

00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:33.820
which connects volunteers
with organizations and projects

00:09:33.820 --> 00:09:35.180
looking for volunteers.

00:09:35.940 --> 00:09:39.620
It, in fact, goes to the extent
of doing a volunteer background check.

00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:43.540
If we can unleash
a “gratitude marketplace” at scale,

00:09:45.260 --> 00:09:50.620
we will create a deep connection
between the traveler and the resident.

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:53.820
Copenhagen is going
on that path with CopenPay.

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:55.700
You get points.

00:09:55.700 --> 00:09:58.940
If you do gardening, you get points.
If you do cycling,

00:09:58.940 --> 00:10:02.580
you can use those points
for redeeming [at] attractions.

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:08.100
If you had the opportunity
to contribute with your time,

00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:09.500
what would you do?

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:11.260
Some of you are animal lovers.

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:16.740
You may want to be part of
the elephant rescue centers in Thailand,

00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:20.660
or want to be part
of sea turtle rescue centers in India.

00:10:21.740 --> 00:10:24.300
If you're an environment or nature lover,

00:10:24.340 --> 00:10:26.700
you may want to be part
of coral reef preservation

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:29.420
in the Great Barrier or in Maldives.

00:10:29.460 --> 00:10:31.500
And if you are a history lover like me,

00:10:33.140 --> 00:10:36.980
you may be wanting
to be a part of restoration

00:10:37.020 --> 00:10:39.100
of an 800-year-old temple like this.

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:44.140
In fact, I will seek such an opportunity
and bake it in my itinerary

00:10:44.180 --> 00:10:47.660
because I will love to be part
of something like this.

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:49.460
The possibilities are infinite.

00:10:51.140 --> 00:10:52.940
The travel industry is going to grow.

00:10:54.540 --> 00:10:59.780
It's one industry that is probably
encouraging tolerance

00:10:59.780 --> 00:11:01.420
in this highly polarized world.

00:11:02.900 --> 00:11:04.180
It's for us

00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:10.860
to shape positively
the destinations we love

00:11:10.860 --> 00:11:13.460
and the people who call it their home.

00:11:15.100 --> 00:11:19.300
I've talked about the tools at hand,
and I've given you a few examples.

00:11:19.340 --> 00:11:22.780
I want to leave with one question.

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:28.700
On your next trip, will you be
a tourist or a joyful guest?

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:32.900
It's time we bring joy back in travel.

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:34.180
Thank you.

00:11:34.220 --> 00:11:36.460
(Applause)

